PHASE 23 — Bilingual Arabic/English Website, RTL/LTR, and Localization QA

Goal:
Make the entire web platform professionally bilingual in Arabic and English, with correct RTL/LTR support.

Important:
Previous phases may have basic language support. This phase is a dedicated localization and language quality pass.

What to build/improve:
- Complete Arabic/English language system across public website, Owner dashboard, Student portal, Parent portal, Academy portal, checkout, onboarding, level checks, homework, reviews, settings, and notifications.
- Language switcher.
- Persistent language preference per user.
- Public visitor language preference using cookie/local storage.
- RTL layout for Arabic.
- LTR layout for English.
- No broken tables/forms/cards in RTL.
- No mixed-direction text issues for Arabic + English content.
- Neutral Arabic UX copy, not female-only.
- Native-level English UX copy.

Pages to audit:
- Public website
- Pricing
- Checkout
- Thank-you
- Student form
- Level check
- Booking calendar
- Student portal
- Parent portal
- Academy portal
- Owner dashboard
- Homework/scenarios/reviews/materials
- AI tools
- Settings
- Notifications
- Emails/WhatsApp templates

Arabic copy rules:
- Avoid exclusively feminine forms like: اكتبي / سجّلي / اختاري
- Use neutral forms like: اكتب / سجّل / اختر
- Keep copy clear, warm, and professional.
- Avoid robotic literal translation.

English copy rules:
- Use natural SaaS-style English.
- Keep CTAs clear and action-oriented.
- Avoid long paragraphs inside forms.

Acceptance criteria:
- User can switch Arabic/English.
- Language preference persists.
- Arabic pages render RTL correctly.
- English pages render LTR correctly.
- All major UI labels are translated.
- No broken layout in Arabic.
- No female-only Arabic copy.

Manual test checklist:
- Switch to Arabic and browse all main flows.
- Switch to English and browse all main flows.
- Test checkout in both languages.
- Test student dashboard in both languages.
- Test parent portal in both languages.
- Test Owner dashboard in both languages.
- Test mobile view in Arabic and English.

